@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+name: accuracy-first
+description: >
+  Project rule for this bsnes-hd fork: hardware-accurate SNES emulation is the core
+  competency and always takes precedence. Modern layers (32-bit/true color, widescreen,
+  HD smoothing, HD windowing, extra Mode 7 options) are optional and must not replace
+  the 15-bit accurate path. Use when implementing or planning PPU, color, videoFrame,
+  blending, widescreen, true color, 32-bit color, defaults, or accuracy tradeoffs.
+  Use when the user runs /accuracy-first.
+---
+
+# Accuracy first
+
+bsnes's value is hardware accuracy. This fork may add a modern layer on top. If an enhancement costs accuracy, it is optional. The accurate workflow must always exist, remain correct, and take precedence.
+
+## Hardware fact
+
+The SNES PPU does not have 32-bit color. CGRAM is 15-bit RGB (5-5-5, 32768 colors). Color math (add/sub/half) and master brightness operate on those 5-bit channels. Official `ppu-fast` matches that: `Pixel.color` is `uint16`, `blend()` uses the 15-bit add/sub algorithm, `lightTable` and `videoFrame` stay 16-bit. That is the accurate path, not a missing feature.
+
+DerKoun hd converted to 24-bit (`uint32`) early so averaging and smoothing had extra precision. That changes color math. Official rejected a whole-pipeline rewrite for that reason.
+
+## Rules
+
+1. **Accurate path is the product default.** Settings, code paths, and frame format match official/hardware behavior unless the user has opted into an enhancement.
+2. **Enhancements sit beside the accurate path, never instead of it.** Gate with a setting. Off = official behavior, including color format and color math. Do not delete, `#if`-out, or "simplify away" the 15-bit `blend()` / `uint16` framebuffer.
+3. **Do not make a modern layer a required foundation.** 32-bit color is not a prerequisite for widescreen. If an effect needs extra precision, that effect is optional too. Do not convert the whole PPU to `uint32` as the only compile-time pipeline.
+4. **Do not silently change precision.** Color math, blending, dither, brightness, and output depth stay hardware-accurate on the default path.
+5. **Pattern:** official HD Mode 7 (`Scale: 1` = native 240p; higher scales optional). Follow that for true color, widescreen, smoothing, and windowing.
+
+## When implementing color or video
+
+- Keep official `uint16` `Pixel.color`, `lightTable`, `output`, and `Platform::videoFrame(const uint16*, ...)` working.
+- If 24-bit conversion exists, it is behind a setting; when off, 15-bit `blend()` still runs.
+- Widescreen, `bgGrad`, HD windowing, and SSAA must not force 32-bit on. Effects that only work in 24-bit stay disabled on the accurate path.
+- Prefer a runtime branch over a second forked PPU, but two complete paths beat one inaccurate path.
+
+Check this skill before changing PPU pixel types, `videoFrame`, blending, or enhancement defaults.
