+++ b/STRATEGY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# bsnes-hd fork strategy
+
+**Status**
+
+- Phase 0 complete (2026-08-23)
+  - `legacy-hd` = DerKoun hd (`fc26b25ea`)
+  - `master` = official bsnes + Linux viewport fix
+- Phase 1 in progress on branch `phase-1-widescreen`
+  - hd `ppu-fast` overlay, widescreen config/UI, 32-bit video path
+  - builds standalone; not committed yet
+- Next: verify SMW / F-Zero / HyperZone / FF3, then commit
+
+Do **not** merge official bsnes into the current hd git history. Port hd’s remaining features onto current official `master` instead.
+
+That is the whole strategy. The “five-year merge” is a much smaller PPU job than it looks, and the maintainer’s objections map cleanly onto what should stay in the fork vs what is worth offering upstream later.
+
+## Why not `git merge`
+
+DerKoun’s repo is **snapshot imports** (`bsnes107r1`, `beta10 (bsnes114)`, …), not a history-preserving fork. There is no merge-base with `bsnes-emu/bsnes`. A real merge is not possible.
+
+What *is* possible is a tree-level port, and the numbers are good:
+
+| | Official `ppu-fast` since v114 (2020) | hd’s `ppu-fast` vs that same v114 |
+|---|---|---|
+| Size | **~80 lines** (mosaic, offset-per-tile, a few serialization bits) | **~800 lines added / ~350 removed** |
+
+Five years of official work is almost entirely **outside** the HD PPU: SameBoy, coprocessor timing, Qt 6, GTK2 removal, ruby/audio driver order, docs. Official already has HD Mode 7, perspective correction, and supersampling — credited to DerKoun.
+
+So the hope that some concerns are already addressed is half right: Linux GUI and a pile of accuracy work *are* already on official master. Widescreen, true color, HD windowing, `.bso` overrides, and the game-fix pack are **not**.
+
+## What official already took vs what is still “hd”
+
+**Already in official bsnes**
+
+- HD Mode 7 scale
+- Perspective correction
+- Supersampling
+- Mosaic (simpler boolean, plus later higan mosaic fixes)
+
+**Still unique to the fork** (this is the overlay)
+
+- Widescreen (per-layer BG, sprites, markers, ignore-window, stretch-window)
+- True color (`Pixel.color` is `uint32` in hd, `uint16` in official)
+- Line-color smoothing (`bgGrad`)
+- HD windowing (`windRad`, prototype)
+- `.bso` setting overrides + `pack/` game fixes
+- Doubled VRAM for widescreen patches
+- Libretro target with all of the above options
+
+Widescreen is the product. True color is the invasive pipeline change. HD windowing is the piece even DerKoun called a prototype.
+
+## Maintainer concerns ([issue 16](https://github.com/bsnes-emu/bsnes/issues/16))
+
+Screwtapello (current maintainer) was not hostile. He was selective:
+
+1. **Same philosophy as byuu.** HD Mode 7 is “the SNES process at higher resolution,” so it went in. Widescreen invents columns the PPU never produced (sprites/HUDs break unless you ROM-hack). That is the least likely thing to be accepted upstream. It is also the reason this fork exists.
+2. **True color (15-bit → 24-bit moved early).** He did not want a whole-pipeline rewrite. He was open to *optional* smoothing, and wondered whether interpolating in 15-bit would be enough for some gradients.
+3. **HD windowing.** DerKoun said it looks bad on tops/bottoms and near-horizontal edges, and the code is naive averaging plus piled-on special cases. Screwtapello’s ask: a *simple* interpolation people can turn off, not a pile of tweaks. Do not offer the current code as a PR.
+4. **Struct-of-arrays / perf rewrites.** Only with measurements. No numbers, no merge.
+5. **GPU Mode 7.** Interesting, “radical replumbing.” He suggested dumping PPU state for a frame and prototyping in a standalone renderer first.
+
+That is a fork-first plan with optional, small upstream PRs later — not “get hd merged into bsnes.”
+
+## Recommended sequence
+
+### Phase 0 — new base (do this first)
+
+Keep current `master` as `legacy-hd` (reference + bisect). Make a new `master` at `official/master`. That remote is already added on the local clone.
+
+You immediately inherit Qt 6, no GTK2, SameBoy updates, coprocessor/PPU accuracy, and official’s Linux audio driver order (Pulse, ALSA, OpenAL — not SDL3). Then we find out which Linux/audio problems actually remain.
+
+### Phase 1 — widescreen overlay
+
+Port `hdtoolkit.hpp`, the extra Mode 7 config fields, and the `ppu-fast` widescreen hooks (`line.cpp` is the bulk of the +400-line delta). Goal: SMW / F-Zero / HyperZone / FF3 look like current hd. This is the hard visual work and the whole point of the fork.
+
+### Phase 2 — true color + line-color smoothing
+
+`uint16` → `uint32` `Pixel.color`, early conversion, `bgGrad`. Keep it behind a setting, default on to match hd. This is the change Screwtapello flinched at; isolating it is how we can talk to him later with a small diff instead of a rewrite.
+
+### Phase 3 — HD windowing, last, default off
+
+Port as-is for parity, labeled experimental. Rewrite only if we care; do not take it upstream in its current form.
+
+### Phase 4 — Linux / audio, after the rebase
+
+Official never grew an SDL3 audio path for standalone bsnes (`ruby` is still ALSA/Pulse/OpenAL). If the issues are “old hd on modern Linux,” Phase 0 may already fix them. If we want SDL3, that is new work (ares is the existence proof), not something we merge from official.
+
+### Phase 5 — performance, after we are on current master
+
+HD’s cost is mostly `(256 + 2×widescreen) × scale²` software pixels. GPU Mode 7 is the real fix and is a research project, which matches both DerKoun and Screwtapello. First: profile the rebased tree; do not optimize the 2020 snapshot.
+
+## What to say to the maintainer, when we have something
+
+Not “please merge the fork.” Three possible later PRs, in his language:
+
+- True-color line smoothing as an **optional** enhancement, with before/after shots and a note that 15-bit-only interpolation was considered.
+- Any actual accuracy/perf fix we find while porting (mosaic is already updated on his side — do not fight that).
+- Benchmarks if we try SoA or other PPU layout changes.
+
+Leave widescreen in this fork. Leave HD windowing out of PRs until it is a simple, optional interpolator.
+
+## Next step
+
+Phase 0 is done. Phase 1 is a surgical port of the ~800-line `ppu-fast` overlay onto current `master`, using `legacy-hd` as the reference.
